      "writtenOn": "2023-08-16T15:58:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What I read in the process - `To do so, you may try to use the “Cherry Pick To” button in the Gerrit UI for the original patch in master`; `The backport must match the master commit` - so all tells, that you need to ensure that backport is a clean cherry-pick from the master, rather then from the previous cherry-pick.\nAlso, frankly speaking, I see no difference in that as long as cherry-picks are clean from master both to N-1 and N-2. Difference would be if cherry-pick to N-1 is not clean, then backport to N-2 indeed worth to be done from N-1, as it might be a clean one.\n\nBackport examples tell only, that N-1 branch backport should be merged before N-2. but it doesn\u0027t say that N-2 should be made from N-1 rather then master, IMO.\n\nIt could be that I just don\u0027t see what you\u0027re referring to in the doc (I did that twice today already - apparently I\u0027m getting blind)...",
